  "body": "# Origin 0.7.6: Shared model continuity and safer project work\n\n2026-10-21\n\n## Conversations finish loading\n\nA late thread update cannot leave a conversation locked while it waits for its messages. Origin reloads the exact conversation, rejects replies from an older selection and lets you retry by selecting the same agent or thread.\n\n## Ordered model backups\n\nChoose up to five backup models for an agent, including supported teammate sources. Opt-in fallback follows that order after a confirmed quota refusal before any reply or action. Partial work is never replayed automatically, and paid API backups need separate consent.\n\n## Daily API budgets\n\nSet a daily USD limit for this computer and optional agent limits, with a reset time zone. Supported API requests reserve their maximum cost before sending; uncertain costs keep their reservation. Unpriced Studio generations, paid transcription and AI calls stop when an applicable limit is active, including Studio workflows.\n\n## Opt-in teammate model sources\n\nOwners can share supported model accounts with selected projects. Choices identify the owner and computer, keep credentials on that computer and require it to be online. Hosted work checks project access, monthly limits and the owner's daily API limits, with leases that prevent uncertain work from silently moving to another account.\n\n## Shared identity and project order\n\nJoining from another computer preserves existing shared Chiefs and agents. Project ordering follows the workspace across members, while private projects and read-only permissions keep their boundaries.\n\n## Specialists keep their conversations\n\nAgents lists specialists without the project Chief. Independent threads and delegated work stay separate, Chief follow-ups return to the same delegated child, and notifications open the exact conversation with a link back to its project thread.\n\n## Minimal Usage and chat layouts\n\nOpen quota and reset details beside the model selector, with context details available on demand. Hidden conversations cannot open a second Usage panel. Compact, Medium and Wide layouts keep the composer and conversation aligned.\n\n## Safer Publish account selection\n\nPublish waits for confirmed channel connections and an available selected account. Removing an extra account cannot silently post through another one. Drafts and approvals remain available while connections are unavailable.\n\n## Narrow windows stay usable\n\nMonthly budget details fit behind a compact control. Studio Design keeps Layers and Design controls reachable while its tools scroll, without moving the canvas or hiding the panel controls.\n\n## Claude API connections\n\nThe dedicated Claude API connection keeps its saved key when the workspace also uses that key for other Claude agents. Connections using an API key report metered billing even when a separate CLI sign-in reports a subscription.\n\n## Project boundaries and private errors\n\nPrivate project budgets require project access. Studio preserves caller identity and budget checks across workflow steps, and integration errors remove configured credentials before reaching shared data or chat.\n\nDesktop source: [origin-v0.7.6](https://github.com/z4mbo/Origin/tree/origin-v0.7.6) (`eb829c152ce3cd4359eeb58bca3dd2e55abff879`). [Native build and packaged smoke checks](https://github.com/z4mbo/Origin/actions/runs/39676135188) completed for Windows x64 and both Mac architectures.\n\nThe Windows portable archive is `Origin-0.7.6-windows-x64.zip`; `Origin-0.7.6-x64.zip` is the Mac Intel update archive. The versioned SHA256SUMS and release manifest bind all thirteen payloads to their source, native run, sizes and hashes.\n\nSigning status, package inspection and remaining platform/provider limits belong to the separately retained delivery evidence. Packaged smoke checks do not establish physical Mac installation, real-provider invoice accounting or an installed owner-profile updater journey. See the [candidate acceptance report](https://github.com/z4mbo/Origin/blob/eb829c152ce3cd4359eeb58bca3dd2e55abff879/docs/verification/origin-candidate-054.md).\n"
